/-!
# The static equivalence of the candidate presentation

The presented candidate (`PrimeCandidates.LanguageDef.language`, the probe)
has one authored equation, `prime-quote (prime-drop name) = name`, and
declares no bag, no set and no collection algebra.  The same holds of its
extension with choice (`probeWithChoice`).  For every language of that kind
(`QuoteDropOnly`) this module reads the static equivalence off the syntax.

* One generator of the equivalence relates a pattern and its quoted dropping,
  in one of the two directions (`QuoteDropOnly.generator`).
* `contract` removes every quotation of a dropping, innermost first.  It is
  constant on the classes of the static equivalence
  (`QuoteDropOnly.contract_eq`): two patterns with different contractions
  are apart.
* `weight` counts the nodes of a pattern other than the quotations and the
  droppings of one pattern.  It is positive, constant on the classes
  (`QuoteDropOnly.weight_eq`), and a context adds the weights of what fills
  its holes (`weight_fill`).

Hence **the contexts of such a presentation have a linear size**
(`QuoteDropOnly.linearSize`): the generated context theory receives no map
from a theory that discards or copies.

The second fact about the statics is an asymmetry.  The equation identifies
`prime-quote (prime-drop name)` with `name`; nothing identifies
`prime-drop (prime-quote atom)` with `atom`
(`dropped_quoted_ne_contract`).
-/

set_option autoImplicit false

namespace Mettapedia.Languages.MeTTa.PrimeComparisons.HostingStyles

open Mettapedia.Logic.HostingStyles

open Mettapedia.GSLT
open Mettapedia.GSLT.LanguageDef
